{
  "sn12.61:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.61 ",
  "sn12.61:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "sn12.61:0.3": "Unlearned ",
  "sn12.61:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn12.61:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. … ",
  "sn12.61:1.3": "“Mendicants, an unlearned ordinary person might become disillusioned, dispassionate, and freed from this body made up of the four principal states. ",
  "sn12.61:1.4": "Why is that? ",
  "sn12.61:1.5": "This body made up of the four principal states is seen to accumulate and disperse, to be taken up and laid to rest. ",
  "sn12.61:1.6": "That’s why an unlearned ordinary person might become disillusioned, dispassionate, and freed from it. ",
  "sn12.61:2.1": "But an unlearned ordinary person is unable to become disillusioned, dispassionate, or freed from that which is called ‘mind’ and also ‘sentience’ and also ‘consciousness’. ",
  "sn12.61:2.2": "Why is that? ",
  "sn12.61:2.3": "Because for a long time they’ve been attached to it, thought of it as their own, and mistaken it: ",
  "sn12.61:2.4": "‘This is mine, I am this, this is my self.’ ",
  "sn12.61:2.5": "That’s why an unlearned ordinary person is unable to become disillusioned, dispassionate, or freed from it. ",
  "sn12.61:3.1": "But an unlearned ordinary person would be better off taking this body made up of the four principal states to be their self, rather than the mind. ",
  "sn12.61:3.2": "Why is that? ",
  "sn12.61:3.3": "Th